spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-136-| BR-005 | Outcome classes: transient = browser offline before 
dispatch, HTTP 429, HTTP 401 while the client session is valid → retry automatically; unknown = network 
error/timeout/no response after dispatch, lease expiry, HTTP 5xx → fence (FR-006); session-ended = client auth reports 
signed out / refresh rejected → hold (FR-012); definitive = 403 `NOT_PARTICIPANT` (incl. a missing conversation), 400 
(e.g. `INVALID_REPLY_TARGET`), 413 `CONTENT_TOO_LARGE`, 409 `CLIENT_MESSAGE_ID_REUSED`, sender mismatch, and any other 
4xx except 401/429 → failed, no automatic retry; a stale-generation rejection only means a newer attempt exists and is 
ignored (FR-011). | R1-q5 C, R2-q4 A, R2-q5 A; reviews r2 #2, #11 |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-137-| BR-006 | Expiry: an item not stored 24 h after the user 
pressed send (or after its last manual "Tentar de novo") becomes "expirada" and is never sent automatically; a manual 
"Tentar de novo" sends it with the same key and starts a new 24 h window. | R1-q5 D, R2-q3 B |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-138-| BR-007 | Cancel only for items known not to be stored, with 
no earlier attempt able to commit, and not claimed; a cancelled item is removed in all tabs and never dispatched. | 
R1-q5 B, R2-q7 A; reviews r2 #2, #5, r3 #1 |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-139-| BR-008 | An explicit user sign-out with unsent items 
requires confirmation; confirming deletes that user's outbox; a sign-out not initiated by the user keeps it. 
Cancelling has no side effect. | R2-q5 A, R2-q6 A |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-140-| BR-009 | Typing: only current conversation members join and 
send on a conversation's typing topic; a user's own typing (any session) is never shown to them; an indicator expires 
≤ 5 s after the last signal; the app leaves a conversation's topic within 5 s of the user's removal; residual exposure 
(receive and send) of a tampered removed-member client is bounded by access-token lifetime (D3, D6). | R1-q8 A, D, E; 
R1-q16 E; D3; D6 |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-141-| BR-010 | Mentions: only current members of the conversation 
at first creation, other than the sender, can be mentioned (rooms: members of the room conversation); no 
`@todos`/`@here`. | R1-q10 A, E; R2-q10 A; D4 |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-142-| BR-011 | Desktop-notification eligibility (extends Phase 4): 
toggle on and permission granted; never for the user's own message; the same user must still be signed in and a member 
at emission time (final check without intervening awaits; residual race accepted, D6); never while any tab of the user 
in that browser is visible and viewing that conversation; DM/group: every new message; room: only messages that 
mention the user; at most one notification per message per browser. | R1-q10 B, R1-q16 C/F, R2-q8 A, R2-q9 A–C; 
reviews r2 #9, r3 #3 |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-143-| BR-012 | Polling runs only while a required Realtime stream 
has been unhealthy for more than 30 s and the tab is visible, every 15 s (immediately on becoming visible), and no new 
poll starts once all streams are healthy. | R1-q7 A, R1-q16 D, R2-q12 C |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-144-| BR-013 | Metric log lines contain only closed-enum event 
type and outcome/reason, bounded durations/counts, conversation type, timestamp, and server-derived app version — 
never message text, attachment names, conversation names, user names or emails, user/conversation identifiers, or any 
client-supplied free text. | R1-q12 B, R2-q2, confirmation point 9; review r2 #14 |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-145-| BR-014 | Database rollout: migrations stay local during the 
phase (written + applied locally with recorded rollback SQL); at phase end they are applied to `vhabpcoyypobgasacsko` 
only with explicit owner authorization, followed by catalog readback and a runtime smoke check; the application is 
deployed by the owner after the migrations; rollback is app first, then migrations. | R1-q13 A |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:146:| BR-015 | Tests: only integration (real local 
Supabase/Realtime/API routes) and E2E (real UI, Playwright); no new unit tests; a touched unit test is replaced by 
integration/E2E coverage and deleted, recorded in TRACK. Each new E2E spec counts only after 3 consecutive passing 
runs. | AGENTS.md test policy, R2-q13 A |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-147-| BR-016 | Conversation restore is per browser and per user; a 
different user never inherits it. | R2-q11 A, B, D |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-148-
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-149-## 9. Data and integrations
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-150-
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-151-### Data inputs
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-152-- Composer text, reply target, and mention selections (user 
IDs).
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-153-- Browser connectivity events, Realtime stream status, tab 
visibility, Supabase auth state changes.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-154-- Responses from `POST /api/messages/create` (status and error 
code) and from the fence/lookup call.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-155-
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-156-### Data outputs
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-157-- Browser IndexedDB outbox keyed by application user ID: 
`clientMessageId`, conversation ID, text, reply target, requested mention user IDs, pressed-send time, delivery-window 
start, order, state (waiting / claimed / unknown / failed + reason / expired), attempt generation, claim holder and 
lease expiry. Deleted per BR-007/BR-008; never shared across users.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-158-- Database: attempt-generation state per (sender, 
conversation, `clientMessageId`) so a fenced or stale generation cannot commit; the original submitted composition 
used for replay comparison; mention records written atomically with the message; private typing-topic authorization 
(RLS on `realtime.messages`, `users.supabase_uid = auth.uid()::text` → `users.id` membership); 
`mark_conversation_read` with an internal membership check; `get_unread_counts` without `anon` EXECUTE; rate-limit 
buckets for all create requests and for fence/lookup calls, separate from the insertion quota.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-159-- API: create route sender and attempt-generation fencing, 
winning-insert quota charging, request budget, `clientMessageId` in responses; fence/lookup route for the caller's own 
message only; authenticated, rate-limited, size-bounded metrics route.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-160-- Structured metric log lines (BR-013).
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-161-- Persisted drawer state per user: open flag + active 
conversation ID.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-162-
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-163-### Integrations
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-164-- Supabase Postgres, Realtime (`postgres_changes`, private 
broadcast topics), Auth (server routes use `createSupabaseServerClient` + `auth.getUser()`).
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-165-- Browser APIs: IndexedDB, Web Locks and/or BroadcastChannel 
for cross-tab claims and signals, Notification API (Phase 4), Page Visibility.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-166-- Hosting/Supabase logs as the metrics sink; no new external 
analytics dependency.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-167-
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-168-## 10. Constraints and assumptions
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-169-
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-170-### Constraints
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-171-- Next.js App Router, TypeScript strict, Supabase, TanStack 
Query; reuse existing hooks, repositories, routes, and query keys rather than parallel implementations.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-172-- Identity: RLS compares `users.supabase_uid` with 
`auth.uid()::text`; foreign keys use `users.id`; messages link to rooms through `conversations.room_id`.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-173-- Browsers: Chrome and Edge desktop (automated E2E); Firefox 
desktop (verified). Safari and mobile not required.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-174-- No service worker; background notifications are page-level 
only.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-175-- No message text, names, or identifiers in metrics (BR-013); 
no external analytics service.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-176-- The sign-out confirmation must not change the Presence 
logout sequence (presence-safety rules apply to that touch point).
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-177-- Online database changes only at phase end with explicit 
authorization (BR-014); the hosted app currently runs the pre-Phase-4 build until the owner deploys, so new server 
contracts must stay compatible with that build and with the Phase 4 build until deployment: unkeyed legacy message 
writes and existing RPC/route signatures keep working against the migrated database.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:178:- Repository test policy (BR-015); type-check, lint, and build 
must pass.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-179-- Timing parameters chosen under the owner's delegation (D4) 
and adjustable in planning only with owner approval: claim request timeout 30 s, lease 45 s, metrics batch ≤ 50 events 
/ 16 KB, one metrics delivery in flight, 5 s metrics abort.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-180-
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-181-### Assumptions
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-182-- None beyond the user-confirmed answers and owner decisions 
recorded in `state.md`.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-183-
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-184-## 11. Edge cases and failure modes
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-185-
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-186-| Case | Expected behavior |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-187-|---|---|
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-188-| Tab closed right after pressing send, before server 
confirmation | Item is already in the outbox; on next load it is fenced and delivered once (AC-040). |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-189-| Request stored but response lost | Item becomes unknown; 
fence finds it stored; resolves as delivered; never offered for cancel or expired (AC-038, AC-042). |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-190-| Original create blocked before its INSERT, or still in the 
network, while another tab fences | The fence wins; the older generation can no longer commit; the item is resent once 
or cancelled/expired without a late duplicate (AC-045). |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-191-| Stale fence arrives after a takeover | Rejected as an older 
generation; the newer attempt is unaffected (AC-045). |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-192-| Hung holder when connectivity returns | Its attempt is 
superseded at once; D1 deadline holds (AC-041). |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-193-| Two tabs come online together | One drain claim per 
conversation; only the oldest unresolved item is eligible; no overlapping create requests for that conversation; each 
stored and shown once, in order (AC-005). |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-194-| Owning tab closes or hangs mid-request | Closed or lease 
expired: another tab fences and finishes once; while the lease is live no other tab dispatches (AC-041). |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-195-| Cancel races a claim | Exactly one wins; a cancelled item is 
never dispatched; a dispatched item cannot be cancelled (AC-006). |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-196-| Lost access before reconnect | First item fails definitively 
with text; later items of that conversation wait; other conversations deliver (AC-007). |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-197-| Access regained after failure | "Tentar de novo" delivers 
it, then the waiting items in order (AC-008). |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-198-| Other definitive outcomes (404, 400, 413, 422) and 5xx | 
Definitive → failed with text; 5xx → unknown → fence (AC-046). |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-199-| `CLIENT_MESSAGE_ID_REUSED` | Failed; "Tentar de novo" 
resends the content under a new key, once (AC-043). |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-200-| Server rate limit during drain; concurrent same-key requests 
| Items stay pending, retried automatically; quota charged once per stored message; replays/fences use a separate 
budget (AC-009). |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-201-| Laptop asleep > 24 h | Not-stored items become "expirada"; 
stored ones resolve as delivered (AC-010, AC-042). |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-202-| Offline attachment / voice | Upload failure: per-file error 
+ retry; create failure after upload: Phase 4 composer failure; nothing in the outbox (AC-011). |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-203-| IndexedDB unavailable or write fails | Nothing dispatched; 
text stays in the composer with the storage message (D5) (AC-039). |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-204-| Identical texts sent twice; Realtime arrives before the HTTP 
response | One bubble per message, matched by key (AC-050). |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-205-| Account switched while a drain is paused or a response is in 
flight | Drain stops; no dispatch as the new user; late responses discarded; server rejects any request whose sender 
differs (AC-044, AC-047). |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-206-| Session ends without Sair; other user signs in | Other user 
never sees/sends A's items; A's items drain after A signs in (AC-012). |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-207-| Temporary Auth failure (401 with valid client session) | 
Treated as transient; retried; not held or deleted (AC-012). |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-208-| Sair with unsent items | Dialog; Cancelar has no side 
effects at any entry point; Sair mesmo stops drains everywhere and deletes the outbox; late responses do not resurrect 
items (AC-013, AC-047). |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-209-| Realtime drop < 5 s | No "Reconectando…" banner (AC-014). |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-210-| Only the conversation-list stream fails | Banner after 5 s 
and polling after 30 s follow its health; recovered independently (AC-015, AC-016). |
--
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-267-- AC-024 (FR-023, FR-024, BR-010; must-not R1-q16 F): On the 
real route and local DB: a message mentioning a non-member ID and the sender's own ID stores no mention for either and 
notifies neither; a replay that changes only the requested mention IDs returns `CLIENT_MESSAGE_ID_REUSED` and changes 
nothing; a message whose text contains "@Bruno" typed without selection stores no mention; a forced failure of mention 
storage stores neither the message nor any mention; anon and non-members cannot read mention records; no client can 
insert/update/delete them directly.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-268-- AC-025 (FR-025, BR-011): Given B has notifications enabled 
and permission granted, B's tab hidden or viewing another conversation, when A mentions B in a room, then B receives 
exactly one notification "<A> mencionou você em <sala>" with the full text; clicking opens that room in the drawer; a 
room message without a mention of B produces none.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-269-- AC-026 (FR-025, BR-011; must-not R1-q16 C): Given B has 
notifications enabled, then a DM mention yields exactly one notification; a thread-reply mention yields one; with B's 
two tabs where the hidden tab receives the event first and the visible tab is viewing that conversation, none; A's own 
message yields none for A; with the toggle off, none; a mention across B's two hidden tabs yields exactly one.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-270-- AC-027 (FR-026): Given A's message mentions B, then all 
members see the mention styled distinctly, and only B sees the whole message highlighted with a non-color cue.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-271-- AC-028 (FR-027, BR-013): Given a send, a stream recovery, 
and a polling episode occur, then the metrics route writes structured lines with enum event type/reason, durations, 
and server-derived version; a scan finds no message text, names, emails, or user/conversation IDs; a payload with 
unknown fields, free-text strings, out-of-range numbers, or a forged version produces no such values in the logs; a 
request over 50 events or 16 KB is rejected; requests beyond the per-user rate limit are rejected; an unauthenticated 
request is rejected and produces no metric log line.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-272-- AC-029 (FR-028): Given the metrics route errors, and 
separately hangs, and separately is flooded with sustained traffic, when A sends, goes offline, and reconnects, then 
AC-001/AC-002 behavior and timing hold, at most one metrics request is in flight from A's tab, a hanging metrics 
request is aborted after 5 s, the client buffer never exceeds its bound (oldest events dropped), and no error is shown.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-273-- AC-030 (FR-029): Given user E is not a member of X, when 
`mark_conversation_read` is invoked for E and X through every role that can execute it, then the call is refused and 
E's read state for X is unchanged (integration, local DB).
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-274-- AC-031 (FR-030): Given the `anon` role, when it calls 
`get_unread_counts`, then permission is denied; an authenticated member still gets correct counts (integration, local 
DB).
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-275-- AC-032 (FR-031, BR-016): Given the drawer open on X, when A 
reloads, then it reopens on X; given A lost access to X, then the list opens with no error; given C signs in on that 
browser, then C does not get A's conversation; given the drawer was closed, it stays closed.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-276-- AC-033 (FR-032): The existing Phase 4 messaging E2E 
regression suite and DB integration suite pass after each slice; `npm run type-check`, `npm run lint`, and `npm run 
build` pass.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-277-- AC-034 (BR-014, §10): Every migration of the phase is 
applied locally with recorded rollback SQL; before any online application, the currently hosted build (git ref 
confirmed by the owner) and the Phase 4 build each pass a send/read/unread smoke against the migrated local database 
(legacy unkeyed writes still work); at phase end, after explicit owner authorization, it is applied to 
`vhabpcoyypobgasacsko`, the catalog is read back from that target, and a runtime smoke check passes; the hand-off 
states the app is ready to deploy after the migrations.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-278-- AC-035 (§12): The Supabase/RLS review gate passes for every 
migration, RLS/Realtime policy, repository, and API route change.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:279:- AC-036 (BR-015): Each new E2E spec passed 3 consecutive runs 
in Chrome and in Edge; the key flows (outbox, banner, typing, mentions) were verified in Firefox and recorded; no unit 
test was added; every touched unit test was replaced and deleted, recorded in TRACK.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-280-- AC-037 (FR-014, §13): The banner is announced via a polite 
live region, item states have text labels, and the sign-out dialog and mention list are fully keyboard-operable.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-281-- AC-038 (FR-002, FR-006, BR-004): Given A's create request is 
stored but its response is dropped, then the item becomes unknown, the fence resolves it as delivered without a second 
create, and B sees it once.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-282-- AC-039 (FR-033, R1-q2 A, D5): Given IndexedDB is unavailable 
(and separately a failing outbox write), when A sends a text message, then zero create requests are sent, the text and 
reply target stay in the composer, and "Este navegador não permite guardar mensagens; libere o armazenamento do site" 
is shown.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-283-- AC-040 (FR-001): Given A is online and the create request is 
held, when A closes the tab before the server confirms, then on reopening the app the item is fenced and B sees the 
message exactly once.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-284-- AC-041 (FR-004): Given tab 1 holds the claim and its create 
request is held, then tab 2 sends no create request for that conversation while tab 1's lease is live; when tab 1 is 
closed (and separately when its lease expires while it hangs), tab 2 fences and the message is stored once. Given tab 
1's attempt hangs across an outage, when connectivity returns with that single item pending and quota available, then 
it is delivered within 10 s (D1) and stored once.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-285-- AC-042 (FR-006, FR-009): Given an unknown item whose request 
was actually stored, when A tries to cancel it or its 24 h passes, then no cancel is offered before fencing, the fence 
resolves it as delivered, and it never shows "expirada".
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-286-- AC-043 (FR-007): Given an item rejected with 
`CLIENT_MESSAGE_ID_REUSED`, when A clicks "Tentar de novo", then its content is stored once under a new key and the 
conflicting stored message is unchanged.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-287-- AC-044 (FR-011, BR-001, §12): Given A's drain is paused 
before dispatch and the browser's session switches to C (a member of the same conversation), when the drain would 
resume, then no create or fence request is sent as C; a crafted create or fence request carrying A as expected sender 
with C's session is rejected and stores or fences nothing; an anon fence/lookup is rejected; C fencing or looking up a 
key that belongs to A's message (with C as sender) neither returns A's message nor affects A's attempts.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-288-- AC-045 (FR-006, BR-004): With real local Postgres and the 
real routes: (a) attempt 1's INSERT is blocked (row lock held by the test) while a fence for that key reports not 
stored; on release attempt 1 does not commit; (b) attempt 1's request is held before reaching the server while a fence 
runs; when released it is rejected as stale; (c) a stale fence (older generation) arriving after a newer attempt was 
dispatched is rejected and the newer attempt commits; in every case at most one message is stored (integration + E2E).
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-289-- AC-046 (FR-007, FR-024, BR-005): On the real route: 403 
(missing conversation or not a participant), 400 (invalid reply target), and 413 (content too large) are classified 
definitive in the drawer (failed with text); a 5xx returned after the request reached the server is classified unknown 
and fenced; an unchanged replay after a mentioned recipient left the conversation returns the stored message (not 409) 
and notifies no removed recipient.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-290-- AC-047 (FR-011, FR-013): Given a real create response and a 
real fence response held while the browser switches from A to C, and separately while A confirms Sair mesmo, and 
separately (same identity) while the item is cancelled or superseded by a newer generation, when the responses are 
released, then no A content appears in C's view, no deleted or cancelled item reappears, and no newer claim or attempt 
is changed.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-291-- AC-048 (FR-016): Given a poll response is held while 
Realtime delivers a newer state (a reaction, a receipt, an attachment message, a mention) and older history pages are 
loaded, when the stale poll is released, then the feed keeps the newer state, the loaded pages, and one bubble per 
message.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-292-- AC-049 (FR-025, BR-011; must-not R1-q16 F): Given B is 
mentioned and B's authoritative check has already returned "member" but display is held, when B's app receives B's 
removal signal (and separately when the browser switches to another account) before display, then no notification is 
shown; given the check is held before it runs and B is removed, then no notification is shown.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-293-- AC-050 (FR-034): Given A sends two messages with identical 
text (one plain, one replying to a message) and Realtime delivers each before its HTTP response, then each shows as 
exactly one bubble in both of A's tabs throughout, matched by `clientMessageId`.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-294-
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:295:## 15. Test strategy
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-296-
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-297-- Test levels:
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-298-  - Integration (local Supabase Postgres/Realtime and real API 
routes): sender and attempt-generation fencing incl. stale requests and stale fences (AC-044, AC-045), insertion 
quota, request budget, and fence budget (AC-009), fence/lookup authorization incl. anon and other users' keys (AC-038, 
AC-042, AC-044), outcome classes (AC-046), mention atomicity/validation/replay/RLS (AC-024, AC-046), private 
typing-topic authorization incl. anon/outsider/public topic (AC-019), `mark_conversation_read` membership (AC-030), 
`get_unread_counts` anon revoke (AC-031), metrics route auth, enums, sizes, rate limit, redaction (AC-028).
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-299-  - E2E (Playwright, real UI; two or more real accounts; two 
tabs of one account; a second device as a separate browser context): every other AC. Network shaping only — the app, 
routes, and Supabase stay real: browser-context offline mode; blocking only the Realtime WebSocket or a single stream; 
holding a request or response by delayed pass-through to the real server; dropping a response or replacing it with a 
gateway 5xx after pass-through; disabling IndexedDB or failing its writes in the page (AC-039). Old-build 
compatibility: the hosted and Phase 4 builds are run locally against the migrated database (AC-034). Expiry may use a 
test-controlled clock without changing the product rule.
