spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md-99-## T11 — Identity fencing and session-end hold
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md-100-Reasoning: Shared-browser and account-switch safety (R1-q16 A) 
is its own guarantee across all tabs.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md-101-Task: Before every dispatch and fence the authenticated 
application user must equal the item owner; an identity change or sign-out in any tab stops drains in all tabs; late 
create/fence/lookup responses after a switch, or older-generation/cancelled-item responses under the same identity, 
are discarded without changing any view, item, or claim; items are held only when the client auth state reports the 
session ended and drain after the same user signs in again; another user never sees, sends, or deletes them; a 401 
with a valid client session stays transient.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md-102-Done when: AC-012, AC-044 (client clauses), and AC-047 (switch 
and same-identity clauses) hold in the real UI.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md-103-Verify by: New E2E specs (session cleared/refresh revoked then 
C signs in, paused drain then switch to C, held real create/fence responses released after switch, cancel, or 
supersede) pass 3 consecutive runs in Chrome and Edge; regression suites pass.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md-104-Covers: FR-011, FR-012, BR-001, AC-012, AC-044, AC-047
