spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md-117-## T13 — Realtime stream health, recovery, and connection 
banner
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md-118-Reasoning: Polling, typing recovery, and metrics consume one 
per-stream health model; the banner is its visible output.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md-119-Task: The messages/receipts/reactions and conversation-list 
streams have application-level health and recovery (rejoin after error, timeout, or terminal closure with capped 
exponential backoff; catch-up refetch of the open feed and list on recovery), exposing per-stream health for other 
consumers; the drawer shows "Sem conexão — mensagens serão enviadas quando voltar" immediately when the browser is 
offline and "Reconectando…" when any required stream has been unhealthy > 5 s while online, in a polite live region, 
hiding itself when all are healthy.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md-120-Done when: AC-014 and the messages/list clauses of AC-015 hold.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md-121-Verify by: New E2E specs using T25 (offline context; 3 s drop; 
messages-only and list-only error, timeout, and terminal closure; recorded increasing capped delays; catch-up of B's 
messages and unread counts) pass 3 consecutive runs in Chrome and Edge; `messaging-reconnect-consistency.spec.ts` and 
regression suites pass.
