spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md-126-## T14 — Polling fallback during Realtime outages
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md-127-Reasoning: G3's second half; depends on stream health and has 
its own merge-safety risk (AC-048).
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md-128-Task: While any required stream has been unhealthy > 30 s and 
the tab is visible, the open conversation's new messages, its loaded messages' receipt summaries, any open 
reader-details list, and the conversation list are fetched every 15 s (immediately on becoming visible); none while 
hidden; no new poll once all streams are healthy; merges never duplicate messages or replace newer/enriched state or 
loaded history pages with older data.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md-129-Done when: AC-016 and the AC-048 reaction, receipt, 
attachment, and history-page clauses hold.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md-130-Verify by: New E2E specs (Realtime-only block with HTTP 
working, list-only outage, partial reads by C, hidden/visible, recovery during an in-flight poll with 60 s quiet 
check, held stale poll vs newer reaction/receipt/attachment message with older pages loaded) pass 3 consecutive runs 
in Chrome and Edge; regression suites pass.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md-131-Covers: FR-016, BR-012, AC-016, AC-048
