spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md-135-## T15 — Reliable named members-only typing indicator
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md-136-Reasoning: Client side of G4 on the T5 topic, with its own 
application-level recovery and removal detection.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md-137-Task: Typing travels on the T5 private topic with payload 
limited to user identity and typing flag; the indicator stays visible during continuous typing and disappears ≤ 5 s 
after stop, blur, send, conversation switch, or tab close; names follow FR-018 in direct, group, and room 
conversations; the user's own sessions never show their typing; the typing stream has application-level recovery after 
error, timeout, or terminal closure with capped exponential backoff and exposes its health; the app detects its own 
removal from a conversation through a signal independent of conversation access — including while that conversation is 
not open in the drawer; Realtime caches channel authorization per join, so token refresh and the conversation-list 
stream alone cannot meet the deadline (TRACK T5) — and leaves the topic within 5 s.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md-138-Done when: AC-017, AC-018, AC-019 (E2E removal clause), 
AC-020, and the typing clause of AC-015 hold for each typing-stream failure class.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md:139:Verify by: New E2E specs (15 s continuous typing sampled each 
second, stop/close/switch, 1/2/3+ typists with T24 users, own two tabs + second device, removal of E while subscribed, 
typing-only error, timeout, and terminal closure via T25 with increasing capped delays) pass 3 consecutive runs in 
Chrome and Edge; regression suites pass.
