spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md-144-## T16 — Live cross-device unread, read state, and own messages
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md-145-Reasoning: G5 is observable independently once key correlation 
exists.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md-146-Task: With healthy connectivity, a full or partial read on one 
tab/device updates the same user's unread counts and read state on their other tabs/devices within 5 s, sender receipt 
summaries/details match stored receipts on all the sender's sessions, and messages the user sends appear once on their 
other devices within 5 s, without reload, focus change, or reconnect.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md-147-Done when: AC-021 and AC-022 hold.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md:148:Verify by: New E2E specs with a T24 second-device context pass 
3 consecutive runs in Chrome and Edge; regression suites pass.
