spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md-171-## T19 — Client messaging metrics that never affect messaging
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md-172-Reasoning: Client half of G7; must be proven harmless (FR-028) 
against a failing route.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md-173-Task: The client records send latency (from the original send 
time, including after a manual retry of an expired item), outbox wait, send outcomes by reason, every messaging 
stream's drops/recoveries/outage duration (messages, list, typing), and polling activations/duration in a bounded 
buffer (oldest dropped), delivering fire-and-forget batches (≤ 50 events, ≤ 16 KB, one in flight, aborted after 5 s, 
dropped under overload) to the T6 route; messaging never awaits metrics.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md-174-Done when: AC-028 (end-to-end lines for a send, a stream 
recovery, and a polling episode; raw-log redaction scan clean) and AC-029 hold, and the latency emitted for a manually 
retried expired item is measured from its original send time.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md:175:Verify by: E2E spec producing the three episodes and an 
expired-item manual retry (test clock; controlled original-send and server-confirmation timestamps recorded; emitted 
latency equals their difference within 1 s, distinct from retry-to-confirm time) with a scan of raw T24 server log 
lines, plus failing, hanging, and flooded route runs asserting AC-001/AC-002 timing, ≤ 1 metrics request in flight, 5 
s abort, bounded buffer, no visible error; 3 consecutive runs in Chrome and Edge.
