spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/TRACK.md-44-- On the LOCAL database (migration 
`supabase/migrations/20261007095045_message_send_attempt_fencing.sql`, written + applied locally, NOT online): keyed 
creates go through `public.create_message_attempt`, which checks the key's attempt row 
(`private.message_send_attempts`, PK sender/conversation/key) after its INSERT and holds the row lock to commit, so a 
fenced or older generation never commits and at most one message exists per key; `public.fence_message_attempt` 
returns the stored message or records the new generation (lower generations can no longer commit) and never creates a 
message; the Phase 4 RPC `create_message_with_attachments` keeps its signature and delegates to the guarded function.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/TRACK.md-45-- Writes outside the fenced contract are refused at the 
database: `send_message_as_self` requires `client_message_id IS NULL` (client keyed inserts denied; unkeyed direct 
inserts still work); trigger `messages_client_message_id_immutable` refuses setting/changing/clearing a key or moving 
a keyed message to another conversation/sender for every role (42501); trigger `messages_keyed_insert_fence` fences 
raw keyed inserts (e.g. a Phase 4 server's service-role insert) — allowed only while the key has no fence state, else 
ATTEMPT_SUPERSEDED — and records delivery.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/TRACK.md-46-- Every keyed message has a delivery record (backfill for 
existing keyed messages; fence/replay record untracked ones under the key lock); a keyed message deleted after this 
migration is never re-created (fence → `stored` with `message: null`; generation-carrying create → 410 
MESSAGE_DELETED).
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/TRACK.md-47-- `POST /api/messages/create` accepts `attemptGeneration` (≥1, 
requires key and expectedSenderId) and `expectedSenderId` (users.id; mismatch → 403 SENDER_MISMATCH before anything is 
read/stored/fenced); new `POST /api/messages/fence` (own key only; 401 anon; 200 stored|not_stored; 409 
ATTEMPT_SUPERSEDED for older generations; 403 NOT_PARTICIPANT; never creates). Create/fence responses carry 
`clientMessageId` (top level and on `message`). Original composition stored per key (content, type, replyToId, sorted 
attachmentIds) for replay comparison; T4 adds sorted mention IDs.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/TRACK.md-48-- Status codes: missing conversation 403 NOT_PARTICIPANT (was 
404) on create/fence only; non-UUID ids 400 (was 500); unchanged keyed replay whose reply target was later deleted → 
200 (was 400). Generation-less keyed creates (Phase 4 client) keep create/replay 200/409 and lose to fence state (D4); 
unkeyed creates unchanged.
