spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/TRACK.md-260-- New `POST /api/messages/metrics`: body `{ events: 
MessagingMetricEventInput[] }`, each `{ type, reason?, conversationType?, durationMs?, count?, occurredAt? }`. Order: 
auth via `requireAuthUser` (401, nothing charged, no metric line) → per-user fail-closed budget 'messaging:metrics' 
30/60 s charged on every authenticated request (429 on limit, limiter failure, or limiter client construction failure) 
→ 415 non-JSON → 413 METRICS_PAYLOAD_TOO_LARGE for raw bodies > 16384 bytes counted on bytes received (declared 
oversize refused before reading; chunked/understated cut while streaming, stream cancelled) → 400 invalid 
UTF-8/JSON/shape → 413 METRICS_BATCH_TOO_LARGE for > 50 events → 202 `{accepted, dropped}`; unexpected errors 500 with 
the error name only. Rejected requests write no metric line (normal api_error diagnostics may still be written).
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/TRACK.md-261-- Closed enums in `src/lib/messaging/metrics-contract.ts` 
(client-shareable; path constant for T19): types send_latency, outbox_wait, send_outcome, messages/list/typing 
_stream_drop and _stream_recovery, polling_start, polling_stop (stream folded into type — compatible with BR-013); 
send_outcome reasons delivered, offline, network_error, timeout, rate_limited, server_error, lost_access, expired, 
invalid_request, content_too_large, key_reused, sender_mismatch, session_ended, cancelled; drop reasons error, 
timeout, closed, offline; conversationType direct/group/room (not on list_* events). Bounds: durationMs integer 
0..max(0, now + 24 h − 2026-01-01) (chosen accepted-clock policy; no fixed ceiling, so delayed manual retries keep 
their latency); count 0..10000 only on *_recovery and polling_stop; occurredAt epoch-ms in [2026-01-01, now + 24 h]. 
Whole event dropped on unknown type, missing required or invalid/not-allowed field; unknown fields ignored; client 
appVersion ignored.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/TRACK.md-262-- Log line (one `console.info` JSON line per accepted event): 
