8: // Nothing is filtered, redacted, or reformatted: every stdout and stderr line is
9: // written byte for byte as the server printed it. The only processing is
10: // line-atomic interleaving: each stream is buffered up to its next newline and
11: // only whole lines are written, so a stdout line and a stderr line never splice
12: // into one another. When a stream ends with an unterminated fragment, the
13: // fragment is written followed by a line feed (0x0a) — the one byte the tee ever adds — so
14: // the next line of the other stream still starts on a line of its own. This is
15: // a local test aid only; the log file lives in an ignored directory and is never
