## T27 — Unknown-outcome recovery through the fence
Reasoning: Review r1 #3, #14: fenced recovery is a separate failure surface from durable enqueue, and AC-040 needs it.
Task: An attempt that ends without a usable response (network error after dispatch, timeout, 5xx after reaching the 
server, tab closed mid-request) leaves the item unknown; before any cancel, expiry, or redispatch the app fences it 
under a new generation; a stored result resolves as delivered (never cancelled or expired); a not-stored result only 
permits the transition that was requested — cancel and expiry complete without any create, and redispatch happens only 
while the item is still current, eligible, and inside its delivery window; cancel is offered only for items known not 
stored; a fence answered 403 `NOT_PARTICIPANT` (access lost while the item was unknown) makes the item failed per 
BR-005 with its text kept, stops automatic attempts, and is never treated as not stored (no expiry, no cancel) — 
"Tentar de novo" fences under a new generation first, so a stored result resolves as delivered and a not-stored result 
follows the normal rules, and "Apagar" only removes the local item.
Done when: AC-003, AC-038, AC-040, AC-042, and the AC-046 5xx clause hold in the real UI with real routes, an unknown 
item fenced as not stored after its 24 h window expires without any create request, and an unknown item whose fence 
returns 403 is failed (not expired, not delivered, not re-created) for both a committed-but-response-lost message and 
a not-yet-stored one.
